& [Reconciliation] means one typed relation, not repair
  + accepted meaning is validation that two supplied carriers are comparable followed by one exact equality disposition
  + it preserves both operands and does not alter either
  + it does not merge, normalize, select, repair, deduplicate, sort, or produce a preferred inventory
  + it does not settle a dispute between agents or grant policy authority

& [Pair] means exactly two output-only carriers
  + cardinality is exactly two and roles are left and right
  + the pair is not a set because order and complete operand identity are retained
  + the pair is not a sequence of physical observations because acquisition is absent
  + no third, optional, empty, raw, or variadic form exists

& [LeftAndRight] mean API positions only
  + left is the first supplied complete operand
  + right is the second supplied complete operand
  + position is inspectable provenance in the result
  + left does not mean earlier, baseline, trusted, authoritative, expected, or preferred
  + right does not mean later, candidate, untrusted, changed, observed, or subordinate

& [CurrentRederivation] means present pure-authority replay
  + current names the version of the already signed prerequisite functions compiled into this program
  + rederivation clones each retained plan and assembly and invokes that public prerequisite transform
  + exact complete carrier equality is required
  + current does not mean recently acquired, fresh from disk, temporally current, or physically reobserved
  + replay creates no new physical evidence

& [Comparable] means exact semantic scope agreement
  + both carriers have current exact result, encoding, retained-plan, and assembly profiles
  + both retained assemblies have equal complete TopologyScanLimits
  + both root observations name one common structural and strong identity scope
  + comparability is a prerequisite for either Equal or Different
  + comparability does not mean physical co-location, simultaneous observation, common handle, common process, or same scan event

& [Scope] has three roles
  + profile scope fixes result, encoding, plan, and assembly vocabularies
  + capability scope fixes complete TopologyScanLimits
  + root identity scope fixes empty relative path, RootDirectory kind, volume serial, and file ID
  + other root fields remain committed inventory content rather than scope
  + correlation and lineage identifiers remain retained but are not scope

& [Limits] mean declared ceilings, not observed completeness
  + equality requires exact complete TopologyScanLimits equality
  + equal ceilings allow comparable supplied claims
  + equal ceilings do not prove either input reached, exhausted, or fully covered those ceilings
  + unequal ceilings are incomparable even when the observed sequences happen to match
  + no arithmetic or set operation combines limits

& [RootIdentity] means supplied common subject identity
  + relative path and kind establish root structural role
  + volume serial and 128-bit file ID establish strong supplied identity
  + this relation depends on prerequisite validation and retained values
  + it does not refresh the identity or prove present physical existence
  + changing other root observation fields remains a valid sequence Difference

& [Equal] means exact digest-value equality under one profile
  + both operands are already comparable and currently rederived
  + ordered_inventory_sha256 lowercase strings are byte equal
  + the claim is qualified by the exact common encoding profile and ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + it denotes equal canonical encoded observation sequences only at the supplied evidence grade
  + it does not denote object equality, lineage equality, plan identity equality, physical byte equality, temporal continuity, completeness, or admission

& [Different] means exact digest-value inequality under one profile
  + both operands remain valid and comparable
  + ordered_inventory_sha256 values differ by at least one byte
  + it is an ordinary disposition, not a validation fault
  + it does not identify which observation or field differs
  + it does not prove a physical mutation, writer, cause, direction, or time

& [Fault] means comparison cannot truthfully complete
  + malformed plan, invalid identity, failed current rederivation, profile mismatch, limit mismatch, root mismatch, resource breach, or internal contradiction is a fault
  + fault is distinct from Different
  + nested left and right digest faults preserve causal position
  + a fault releases no partial scope or disposition

& [CorrelationIdentity] remains nonsemantic to equality
  + reconciliation_identity binds the caller request and output
  + commitment_identity binds each prerequisite digest request
  + assembly_identity, projection_identity, and entry_reference_identity bind lower workflows
  + unequal correlation identities do not by themselves make supplied sequences Different or incomparable
  + all remain retained through complete operand lineage

& [Order] has two distinct meanings
  + ordered_inventory order is committed inside each digest and is semantic sequence content
  + left-right argument order is retained output provenance and not digest content
  + neither meaning establishes physical acquisition time
  + no sorting, canonical operand order, or repair is permitted

& [Stable] is deliberately unavailable
  + stability requires a relation across observed states with a justified temporal or lifecycle frame
  + two supplied values contain no independent observation of time or source
  + Equal therefore cannot be named stable in this slice
  + future physical authority may wrap this result and add a proven temporal role without changing this meaning

& [DoubleInventory] is future physical evidence
  + it requires two actual inventory acquisitions bound to one physical subject and an exact order
  + it requires producer provenance and completeness semantics not present here
  + supplied pair cardinality alone is insufficient
  + no result, enum, field, test, or document in this slice may claim double inventory

& [QuiescentDoubleInventory] is a stronger future grade
  + it additionally requires process exit, descendant accounting, writer uncertainty, repository state, and capture-bound observations
  + equal physical inventories still retain residual uncertainty unless stronger snapshot primitives are proven
  + this slice supplies neither process nor filesystem evidence
  + Equal is never an alias for quiescent_double_inventory

& [OutputOnly] means construction lineage is closed
  + prerequisite digest carriers cannot be deserialized or publicly constructed
  + reconciliation consumes them as complete owned values
  + reconciliation output is also private and Serialize-only
  + output-only prevents raw-input success but does not transform supplied provenance into physical provenance

& [EvidenceGrade] is one precise lattice point
  + canonically_committed is inherited independently for each operand
  + current_rederived is established independently for each operand
  + scope_correlated is established across the pair
  + pair_equal_or_different is established by the disposition
  + physical, temporal, stable, double-inventory, quiescent, receipted, and admitted grades remain absent

& [RefinedRequirementLanguage] is mandatory
  + say left and right, never before and after
  + say Equal and Different, never stable and changed-over-time
  + say comparable supplied sequence commitments, never repeated physical inventories
  + say current pure rederivation, never fresh observation
  + say root scope identity, never proven present filesystem root
  + say exact limits equality, never equal completeness

& [AmbiguityDisposition] is closed
